# #6759 c11 (D-CORE-FILE-ADAPTERS1=A): csv.reader and xml.reader are generic
# over the Prelude `Reader`. A program's own byte source, handing out two or
# three bytes per read, feeds both, and `loop .. in` walks the generic
# readers; a source whose reads fail surfaces as an IO EncodingError whose
# cause keeps the IOError's OS code and its errno kind. The empty `<s/>` is one
# element_start with empty_style "empty" and no element_end (encoding-decisions:
# an empty element emits no element_end). Each tier prints the same lines.
